      "label": "pitying emotion",
      "description": "The emotion expressed is pity, conveyed through the framing of the image and text that portrays the woman as an object of pity or amusement due to her disability, reducing her personal effort to a spectacle for others' consumption.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_c677a9fe"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_38aa0e72",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "The text 'down syndrome girl' maps onto the visual entity of the woman with Down syndrome.",
      "description": "The text explicitly identifies the visual subject as a 'down syndrome girl', creating a direct analogical mapping between the textual label and the visual entity. This mapping is central to the meme's harmful intent, as it reduces the woman to her disability and frames her actions through the lens of pity or amusement.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_c677a9fe"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8af929cd",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual material identifying the woman as a 'down syndrome girl'",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'down syndrome girl put' which explicitly labels the visual subject by her disability. This projection frames the user's perspective as one that categorizes and reduces the woman to her disability, aligning with the meme's harmful intent of infantilization and pity narrative. The user is not directly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the textual labeling creates an implicit projection where the viewer is positioned as someone who interprets the woman's actions through the lens of her disability, reinforcing ableist stereotypes.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_c677a9fe"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
